ered that shattering AJ\u0027s personal worldview *before* Trimmel\u0027s systemic one would be more impactful. However, this has drawbacks like disrupting the current narrative flow and potentially making AJ too cynical. I\u0027m now exploring the implications of Trimmel\u0027s realization points and what he observes in Stalliongrad and the Crystal Empire.\n\n\n**Unveiling The Trap**\n\nI\u0027m now zeroing in on the pivotal moments that solidified Trimmel\u0027s perception of Chrysalis as a fraud. Blueblood\u0027s logistical skills and the assassination of Thranx were key observations. I\u0027m focusing on how the \"gloat\" advice functions as a test, exposing her narcissism. I now see the \"gloat\" advice as a subversion, a psychological trap. I\u0027m unpacking the implications.",
